<section class="orientation" aria-labelledby="orientation-heading">
  <div class="orientation-lead">
    <p class="section-label">The premise</p>
    <h2 id="orientation-heading">Capability is not destiny.</h2>
    <p>
      The same broad technical capacity could support genuine freedom, familiar
      inequality, private dependency, or severe political repression. The hinge
      is institutional: who owns production, who can contest power, which rights
      remain enforceable, and whether abundance becomes a shared claim.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ol class="orientation-points">
    <li>
      <span>01</span>
      <p>
        <strong>Many futures fit the technology.</strong> Capability does not contain
        a social contract.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>02</span>
      <p>
        <strong>None is inevitable.</strong> The scenarios are conditional equilibria,
        not predictions.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>03</span>
      <p>
        <strong>Present choices change the range.</strong> Institutions can widen
        or close future options.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

